.TH "RPMGRAPH" "1" "2026-03-06" "RPM 6.0.1"
.PP
.SH "نام (NAME)"
rpmgraph \- Generate an RPM Package Dependency Graph
.PP
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBrpmgraph\fR [options] \fIPACKAGE_FILE\fR .\&.\&.\&
.PP
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\fBrpmgraph\fR reads \fBrpm\fR packages passed as arguments, sorts them as
for installation with \fBrpm\fR(8), and produces a dependency graph on
the standard output.\&
.PP
Nodes in the dependency graph are package names, and edges in the
directed graph point to the parent of each node.\& The parent node is
defined as the last predecessor of a package when partially ordered
using the package dependencies as a relation.\& That means that the parent
of a given package is the package'\&s last prerequisite.\&
.PP
The output is in \fBdot\fR(1) directed graph format, and can be displayed
or printed using the \fBdotty\fR(1) graph editor from the \fBGraphviz\fR
project.\&
.PP
.SH ARGUMENTS
\fIPACKAGE_FILE\fR
.RS 4
Either an \fBrpm\fR package or an \fBrpm-manifest\fR(5) file.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
See \fBrpm-common\fR(8) for the options common to all rpm commands.\&
.PP
.SH "وضعیت خروج (EXIT STATUS)"
On success, 0 is returned, a nonzero failure code otherwise.\&
.PP
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBdot\fR(1), \fBdotty\fR(1)
.PP
\fBhttp://www.\&graphviz.\&org/\fR
